            "review_title": "Review at Bún chả 22 ngõ Huyện",
            "review_text": "Sam\nPalm Beach, Florida941 contributions\n0\nFantastic food and local ambiance\nApr 2026 • Solo\nBun Cha 22, Hanoi Old Quarter\nA quick heads-up before anything else: make sure you find the right spot. There are several bun cha places clustered in this part of the Old Quarter, so double-check you're heading to number 22 specifically.\nAnother great back-alley find. I was seated at one of those tiny plastic tables with an equally tiny stool, right next to a fellow solo traveler, and we ended up swapping Hanoi stories over lunch, one of those unplanned, genuinely fun moments that make solo travel worth it. The kitchen and the seating both line the same wall, a setup that says a lot about the resourcefulness and entrepreneurial spirit you see all over Vietnam.\nI got there early, around 11:30, right as things were just ramping up. By the time I left, the place was packed, a solid mix of locals and tourists all waiting for a seat to open up.\nOne local tip worth passing along: bun cha is traditionally a lunch dish. If you find a place serving it at night, it's worth being a little skeptical about freshness. Terrific food and fantastic local ambiance.\nRead more\nWritten July 9, 2026",
